00:00:46.872 --> 00:00:47.974
But we weren't sure if the grand

00:00:48.107 --> 00:00:49.542
jury had met or even that they

00:00:49.675 --> 00:00:50.009
had voted.

00:00:50.142 --> 00:00:52.945
But it has been a relatively

00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:53.813
tranquil scene here today.

00:00:53.946 --> 00:00:54.780
Of course, if you remember back

00:00:54.914 --> 00:00:56.048
in New York after trump was

00:00:56.182 --> 00:00:58.084
indicted on the state charges by

00:00:58.217 --> 00:00:58.751
the Manhattan district

00:00:58.818 --> 00:00:59.618
attorney's office, it was a

00:00:59.752 --> 00:01:00.152
similar thing.

00:01:00.286 --> 00:01:01.420
The indictment came down on a

00:01:01.554 --> 00:01:01.787
Thursday.

00:01:01.921 --> 00:01:03.489
He was arraigned the following

00:01:03.622 --> 00:01:03.823
Tuesday.

00:01:03.956 --> 00:01:04.757
That gave everyone time to get

00:01:04.824 --> 00:01:05.157
into place.

00:01:05.291 --> 00:01:07.660
So you can imagine the scene

00:01:07.793 --> 00:01:09.261
here will become quite busy, not

00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:11.430
only the media descending, but

00:01:11.564 --> 00:01:12.999
also potentially some trump

00:01:13.132 --> 00:01:14.767
supporter, some members of the

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:15.034
public.

00:01:15.167 --> 00:01:16.435
As Evan was just explaining,

00:01:16.769 --> 00:01:18.871
they will have to get a security

00:01:19.005 --> 00:01:19.772
programmer in place here.

00:01:19.905 --> 00:01:21.340
Trump being at mar-a-lago, as

00:01:21.474 --> 00:01:24.276
you well know, they're used to

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:25.611
having him, transporting him

00:01:25.745 --> 00:01:25.945
around.

00:01:26.078 --> 00:01:27.113
But this is certainly of a

00:01:27.246 --> 00:01:29.015
different magnitude and

00:01:29.148 --> 00:01:30.316
dimension, the first time a

00:01:30.449 --> 00:01:33.152
former president facing federal

00:01:33.285 --> 00:01:33.486
charges.

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:34.186
There was this run-through in

00:01:34.320 --> 00:01:36.122
New York.

00:01:36.255 --> 00:01:36.789
We saw how that worked.

00:01:36.856 --> 00:01:38.024
What's unclear here is how they

00:01:38.157 --> 00:01:39.892
will handle it internally.

00:01:40.026 --> 00:01:42.094
Will they shut down the

00:01:42.228 --> 00:01:43.062
courthouse like they did in new

00:01:43.195 --> 00:01:44.230
York, freezing the building,

00:01:44.363 --> 00:01:45.765
freezing the floors that the

00:01:45.898 --> 00:01:46.799
former president was going to be

00:01:46.832 --> 00:01:48.801
on, and then creating a pretty

00:01:48.834 --> 00:01:50.102
rigorous system of who would be

00:01:50.236 --> 00:01:52.004
able to get into the courtroom

00:01:52.138 --> 00:01:53.139
to witness this because there

00:01:53.272 --> 00:01:55.007
are no cameras in court.

00:01:55.141 --> 00:01:56.942
And there are no cameras in

00:01:57.076 --> 00:01:57.510
federal court.

00:01:57.643 --> 00:01:58.444
So the public won't get a

00:01:58.811 --> 00:01:59.045
glimpse of this.

00:01:59.178 --> 00:02:00.446
It remains to be seen how

00:02:00.813 --> 00:02:01.547
they're going figure out the

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.882
logistics of having this

00:02:03.015 --> 00:02:03.783
arraignment take place on

00:02:03.916 --> 00:02:04.417
Tuesday.

00:02:04.817 --> 00:02:04.850
Kaitlan?

00:02:04.984 --> 00:02:06.819
&gt;&gt; Remarkable to see a second

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:07.586
indictment in just such a short

00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:08.387
period of time.

00:02:08.821 --> 00:02:09.789
Thank you, Kara.

00:02:09.922 --> 00:02:11.257
&gt;&gt;&gt; More perspective now.

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.459
Joining me now is our senior

00:02:13.592 --> 00:02:15.394
political correspondent Abby

00:02:15.528 --> 00:02:17.763
Phillip, Paula Reid, chief

00:02:17.897 --> 00:02:18.831
national correspondent John

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:20.399
king, and conservative lawyer

00:02:20.833 --> 00:02:21.734
and "Washington post"

00:02:21.867 --> 00:02:22.468
contributing columnist John

00:02:22.835 --> 00:02:24.136
Conway, who has long predicted

00:02:24.270 --> 00:02:26.038
that this moment would come to

00:02:26.172 --> 00:02:26.338
pass.

00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:27.106
But it's historic.

00:02:27.239 --> 00:02:29.041
&gt;&gt; It is absolutely.

00:02:29.175 --> 00:02:30.843
&gt;&gt; No other president has faced

00:02:30.943 --> 00:02:31.977
federal charges before.

00:02:32.111 --> 00:02:32.945
&gt;&gt; It is absolutely historic.

00:02:33.079 --> 00:02:36.849
This is probably the most

00:02:36.849 --> 00:02:39.952
significant historically -- most

00:02:40.086 --> 00:02:40.853
historicalcally important

00:02:40.886 --> 00:02:44.990
criminal case since the Aaron

00:02:45.124 --> 00:02:46.425
burr case at the beginning of

00:02:46.859 --> 00:02:48.094
the 19th century when he was

00:02:48.227 --> 00:02:48.861
tried for treason.

00:02:48.894 --> 00:02:50.096
It is stunning to see.

00:02:50.229 --> 00:02:51.363
It's breath taking to see, but

00:02:51.497 --> 00:02:52.431
it's not surprising at all.

00:02:52.865 --> 00:02:53.566
The fact of the matter, and

00:02:53.699 --> 00:02:54.867
Donald Trump is going to argue

00:02:54.867 --> 00:02:56.969
that he was mistreated, and he

00:02:57.103 --> 00:02:59.071
is being singled out and he is

00:02:59.205 --> 00:02:59.572
being abuse.

00:02:59.705 --> 00:03:00.973
But the fact of the matter is

00:03:01.107 --> 00:03:02.942
he's gotten the Ben of the

00:03:03.075 --> 00:03:03.242
doubt.

00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:04.510
If you or any of us at this

00:03:04.877 --> 00:03:05.511
table had been a government

00:03:05.644 --> 00:03:06.879
official in the white house

00:03:06.912 --> 00:03:07.513
during the trump administration

00:03:07.646 --> 00:03:09.181
and we took this volume of

00:03:09.315 --> 00:03:11.050
documents home and we jerked

00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:13.085
around the national archives and

00:03:13.219 --> 00:03:15.054
records administration for a

00:03:15.187 --> 00:03:16.322
year and a half plus, and then

00:03:16.455 --> 00:03:18.891
forced the government to get to

00:03:18.991 --> 00:03:19.658
a search warrant, it wouldn't

00:03:19.792 --> 00:03:20.893
have taken a year and a half for

00:03:20.893 --> 00:03:21.894
them to get the search warrant.

00:03:22.027 --> 00:03:24.530
The FBI would have been at our

00:03:24.897 --> 00:03:25.531
doors within months.

00:03:25.664 --> 00:03:28.567
And the fact of the matter is

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:29.268
when this search warrant came

00:03:29.401 --> 00:03:30.402
out, we saw the affidavit.

00:03:30.536 --> 00:03:33.172
We saw a redacted affidavit that

00:03:33.305 --> 00:03:36.041
the FBI used to get the search

00:03:36.175 --> 00:03:38.410
warrant executed at mar-a-lago.

00:03:38.544 --> 00:03:41.213
And the amount of information in

00:03:41.347 --> 00:03:42.281
there was absolutely stunning at

00:03:42.414 --> 00:03:42.915
the time.

00:03:42.948 --> 00:03:44.917
I mean, it was shocking at the

00:03:44.917 --> 00:03:45.217
time.

00:03:45.351 --> 00:03:47.520
That they had such a powerful

00:03:47.653 --> 00:03:48.921
case already.

00:03:48.921 --> 00:03:49.889
Simply by virtue of the fact

00:03:50.022 --> 00:03:52.057
they found the stolen property

00:03:52.191 --> 00:03:55.327
in his office and at his home.

00:03:55.461 --> 00:03:57.796
So the fact of the matter is he

00:03:57.930 --> 00:04:00.332
could have been indicted months

00:04:00.466 --> 00:04:00.599
ago.

00:04:00.933 --> 00:04:02.568
And again, if it was one of us,

00:04:02.935 --> 00:04:03.836
he would have been indicted

00:04:03.969 --> 00:04:04.937
months ago.

00:04:04.937 --> 00:04:06.005
He has gotten special treatment

00:04:06.138 --> 00:04:06.939
in his favor.

00:04:07.006 --> 00:04:08.174
And that is not a criticism of

00:04:08.307 --> 00:04:08.941
the justice department.

00:04:08.941 --> 00:04:10.242
It's a statement of fact that

00:04:10.376 --> 00:04:11.777
the justice department has to be

00:04:11.911 --> 00:04:14.180
extra careful and extra cautious

00:04:14.313 --> 00:04:16.448
and make sure that it has all

00:04:16.582 --> 00:04:18.951
its ducks in a row before

00:04:19.051 --> 00:04:20.553
bringing a charge against the

00:04:20.953 --> 00:04:22.154
former president, a presidential

00:04:22.288 --> 00:04:22.521
candidate.

00:04:22.955 --> 00:04:23.756
But these charges could have

00:04:23.889 --> 00:04:25.024
been brought long ago.

00:04:25.157 --> 00:04:26.258
And one other point.

00:04:26.392 --> 00:04:28.460
On the venue, there has been the

00:04:28.594 --> 00:04:29.528
suggestions that somehow this

00:04:29.662 --> 00:04:31.130
was a sudden change in venue.

00:04:31.263 --> 00:04:33.766
The fact of the matter is we

00:04:33.899 --> 00:04:35.267
knew back in August that there

00:04:35.401 --> 00:04:37.002
was going to be a potential

00:04:37.136 --> 00:04:40.973
venue issue, and people were

00:04:40.973 --> 00:04:43.108
discussing it, legalers were

00:04:43.242 --> 00:04:44.977
discussing it, not in the cafes,

00:04:45.077 --> 00:04:47.112
not in the coffee shops of

00:04:47.246 --> 00:04:48.647
America.

00:04:48.981 --> 00:04:50.449
But there was legals.

00:04:50.583 --> 00:04:51.850
Because so much of the illegal

00:04:51.984 --> 00:04:53.953
conduct that was described in

00:04:54.086 --> 00:04:56.989
the FBI affidavit took place at

00:04:56.989 --> 00:05:00.025
mar-a-lago, in palm beach,

00:05:00.159 --> 00:05:00.993
Florida.

00:05:00.993 --> 00:05:01.527
And the constitution, the sixth

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:02.428
amendment provides that a

00:05:02.561 --> 00:05:03.996
criminal defendant, here Donald

00:05:04.129 --> 00:05:04.997
Trump, the criminal defendant,

00:05:04.997 --> 00:05:07.333
is entitled to a jury in the

00:05:07.466 --> 00:05:09.001
district and the state in which

00:05:09.034 --> 00:05:10.402
he committed the crime.

00:05:10.536 --> 00:05:11.503
&gt;&gt; You mention the justice

00:05:11.637 --> 00:05:11.904
department.

00:05:12.037 --> 00:05:13.005
We haven't heard anything from

00:05:13.072 --> 00:05:14.006
them yet, Paula.

00:05:14.139 --> 00:05:15.874
Do you expect that we will?

00:05:16.008 --> 00:05:18.110
How does the special counsel's

00:05:18.244 --> 00:05:20.479
office handle this?

00:05:20.613 --> 00:05:21.180
&gt;&gt; Yeah, our reporting right

00:05:21.313 --> 00:05:24.516
now, kaitlan is we will not hear

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:25.217
anything from special counsel

00:05:25.351 --> 00:05:26.452
jack Smith or his office.

00:05:26.585 --> 00:05:28.020
That is a deliberate choice.

00:05:28.153 --> 00:05:29.955
They must have known when they

00:05:30.089 --> 00:05:31.023
offered the courtesy of

00:05:31.156 --> 00:05:33.025
informing he had been indicted,

00:05:33.025 --> 00:05:34.627
that's standard, that's what you

00:05:35.027 --> 00:05:35.928
would do with most defendants

00:05:36.061 --> 00:05:37.429
you knew this was very likely to

00:05:37.563 --> 00:05:38.697
wind up on social media, which

00:05:39.031 --> 00:05:40.366
is exactly what happened.

00:05:40.499 --> 00:05:43.469
They're not going to offer any

00:05:43.602 --> 00:05:44.570
statements, any additional

00:05:44.703 --> 00:05:45.638
details or unseal the indictment

00:05:45.771 --> 00:05:47.039
tonight that is her choice.

00:05:47.039 --> 00:05:48.574
But we have to look at how this

00:05:48.707 --> 00:05:51.076
worked out with past special

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:55.481
counsels in terms of letting

00:05:55.614 --> 00:05:56.682
other people craft the

00:05:57.049 --> 00:05:57.182
narrative.

00:05:57.182 --> 00:05:57.783
The justice department and FBI

00:05:57.916 --> 00:05:59.151
have been under siege.

00:05:59.285 --> 00:06:00.185
Criticism about political bias

00:06:00.319 --> 00:06:01.587
from both sides of the aisle for

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:03.922
the past seven or eight years,

00:06:04.056 --> 00:06:05.190
since the investigation into

00:06:05.324 --> 00:06:06.292
Hillary Clinton's use of a

00:06:06.425 --> 00:06:07.259
private email server.

00:06:07.393 --> 00:06:09.061
One of the reasons we have a

00:06:09.061 --> 00:06:09.762
special counsel is because the

00:06:09.895 --> 00:06:10.562
attorney general is trying to

00:06:10.696 --> 00:06:12.398
protect the integrity, right,

00:06:12.531 --> 00:06:14.066
the public's view of the justice

00:06:14.199 --> 00:06:14.466
department.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.167
So tonight the fact that the

00:06:15.301 --> 00:06:16.235
special counsel is not going say

00:06:16.368 --> 00:06:17.403
anything, that we're getting

00:06:17.536 --> 00:06:18.170
most of the breaking news from

00:06:18.304 --> 00:06:19.738
the former president who has

00:06:19.872 --> 00:06:21.240
just been indicted, that is

00:06:21.373 --> 00:06:22.274
something that history will

00:06:22.408 --> 00:06:23.075
ultimately judge.

00:06:23.075 --> 00:06:25.411
It's unclear, though, if this is

00:06:25.544 --> 00:06:26.011
the correct decision.

00:06:26.145 --> 00:06:28.047
&gt;&gt; Although I think we can

00:06:28.180 --> 00:06:30.249
probably say regardless of what

00:06:30.382 --> 00:06:31.550
they said something or not,

00:06:31.684 --> 00:06:32.751
accusations of bias would always

00:06:33.085 --> 00:06:33.285
be there.

00:06:33.419 --> 00:06:35.087
Because this was the plan all

00:06:35.087 --> 00:06:35.287
along.

00:06:35.421 --> 00:06:37.956
Trump and his allies have been

00:06:38.090 --> 00:06:39.925
trying to sow the seeds of doubt

00:06:40.059 --> 00:06:41.093
about whether this case was

00:06:41.093 --> 00:06:42.594
significant or not.

00:06:42.728 --> 00:06:43.762
And notably, even the people who

00:06:43.896 --> 00:06:46.665
are running against him are sort

00:06:47.099 --> 00:06:47.800
of accepting this narrative that

00:06:47.933 --> 00:06:49.401
because he is a former

00:06:49.535 --> 00:06:51.837
president, and because he is

00:06:51.970 --> 00:06:55.107
running for president again,

00:06:55.207 --> 00:06:57.409
that that ought to subject him

00:06:57.543 --> 00:07:01.447
to some other kind of standard.

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:02.181
And that I think is what will be

00:07:02.314 --> 00:07:03.115
tested here once we know the

00:07:03.215 --> 00:07:03.782
details of it.

00:07:03.916 --> 00:07:04.383
The significance of the

00:07:04.516 --> 00:07:07.119
reporting that you and the rest

00:07:07.219 --> 00:07:08.454
of the team reported about that

00:07:08.587 --> 00:07:10.255
tape in which he is talking

00:07:10.389 --> 00:07:14.293
about a specific document, we

00:07:14.426 --> 00:07:15.160
don't know whether that document

00:07:15.294 --> 00:07:16.628
is involved in this.

00:07:16.762 --> 00:07:17.896
We don't know whether that was

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:18.163
all.

00:07:18.297 --> 00:07:19.832
Even if it were alone, I think

00:07:19.965 --> 00:07:22.501
it really opens the door to a

00:07:22.634 --> 00:07:23.902
really serious set of issues

00:07:24.036 --> 00:07:27.539
about national security, about

00:07:27.673 --> 00:07:28.273
trump trying to utilize the

00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:30.109
documents in a way, in any kind

00:07:30.242 --> 00:07:32.778
of way, frankly.

00:07:33.145 --> 00:07:34.747
Not just to peruse them, but to

00:07:35.147 --> 00:07:36.682
prove a point about general mark

00:07:36.815 --> 00:07:37.149
Milley.

00:07:37.149 --> 00:07:39.151
Those are really serious issues.

00:07:39.151 --> 00:07:40.519
And the ones that cannot really

00:07:40.652 --> 00:07:42.254
be spun once we know the

00:07:42.388 --> 00:07:42.621
details.

00:07:42.755 --> 00:07:43.422
&gt;&gt; That's national defense

00:07:43.555 --> 00:07:43.822
information.

00:07:43.956 --> 00:07:46.225
&gt;&gt; We have not heard one word

00:07:46.358 --> 00:07:47.159
publicly from the special

00:07:47.159 --> 00:07:48.260
counsel since he took this job.

00:07:48.394 --> 00:07:49.194
Which if you're talking about

00:07:49.328 --> 00:07:51.163
the grafify of the case,

00:07:51.196 --> 00:07:52.097
investigating a former

00:07:52.231 --> 00:07:54.833
president, the gravity of the

00:07:55.167 --> 00:07:55.634
issues, the you can understand

00:07:55.768 --> 00:07:55.934
that.

00:07:56.068 --> 00:07:57.836
But if you study the lessons of

00:07:57.970 --> 00:08:00.072
the Mueller report, if you study

00:08:00.205 --> 00:08:02.040
the lessons of two impeachments,

00:08:02.174 --> 00:08:04.209
you also understand what Donald

00:08:04.343 --> 00:08:05.177
Trump is going to do and has

00:08:05.177 --> 00:08:05.310
been doing.

00:08:05.444 --> 00:08:07.646
What he has been doing for weeks

